 <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:37:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: let the CAPTURE format be set while OUTPUT
 streams
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The decoder's S_FMT returns EBUSY when either queue is streaming. The
stateful decoder interface (dev-decoder.rst, "Capture Setup") has the
client set the CAPTURE format after the source change event, while the
OUTPUT queue keeps streaming, and Chromium's V4L2 decoder does exactly
that: its S_FMT on CAPTURE failed with "vidioc_s_fmt queue busy" and
it gave up on the stream.

Only refuse a format change on the queue that is streaming.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ángel René <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
index 3d10dcccf..31ddaf074 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
@@ -453,7 +453,13 @@ static int vidioc_s_fmt(struct file *file, void *priv, struct v4l2_format *f)
 	pix_mp = &f->fmt.pix_mp;
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
-	if (vb2_is_streaming(&ctx->vq_src) || vb2_is_streaming(&ctx->vq_dst)) {
+	/*
+	 * Each queue's format is fixed only while that queue streams: the
+	 * stateful decoder interface has the client set the CAPTURE format
+	 * after the source change event, with OUTPUT still streaming.
+	 */
+	if (vb2_is_streaming(f->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE ?
+			     &ctx->vq_dst : &ctx->vq_src)) {
 		v4l2_err(&dev->v4l2_dev, "%s queue busy\n", __func__);
 		ret = -EBUSY;
 		goto out;
